## 2. Phase 1 — Super-deep primary-source research

Research must be current. Open official docs and check the relevant version/release/date before making recommendations. Keep a research log with source, publisher, URL, access date, publication/release date where available, evidence summary, relevance, limitations, and the decision influenced.

### Required primary-source starting points

Re-check current official URLs and version status before relying on them:

1. npm package publishing and package metadata: https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/ and https://docs.npmjs.com/creating-and-publishing-unscoped-public-packages/
2. npm package `package.json` fields, access, trusted publishing, and provenance: https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/configuring-npm/package-json, https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers/
3. Node package exports and resolution: https://nodejs.org/api/packages.html
4. TypeScript package declarations and publishing: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/declaration-files/publishing.html
5. Vite library mode: https://vite.dev/guide/build.html#library-mode
6. Tailwind CSS v4 theme variables and sharing tokens across projects: https://tailwindcss.com/docs/theme
7. pnpm workspace concepts: https://pnpm.io/workspaces
8. npm workspaces, if relevant: https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/using-npm/workspaces
9. Changesets versioning and publishing: https://changesets.dev/guide/versioning-and-publishing
10. GitHub Actions security hardening: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/security-for-github-actions/security-guides/security-hardening-for-github-actions
11. npm trusted publishing: https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers/
12. shadcn/ui registry overview and setup: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/registry and https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/registry/getting-started
13. Storybook documentation for component-library docs: https://storybook.js.org/docs/writing-docs
14. React and TypeScript current guidance: https://react.dev/ and https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/
15. Design Tokens Community Group specification, for the token package boundary: https://www.designtokens.org/tr/2025.10/ and/or the current W3C Community Group report page.
16. GitHub Releases and release automation docs, if releases are in scope: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/releasing-projects-on-github
17. npm package provenance/supply-chain guidance and OpenSSF material where applicable.

Also research alternatives only when relevant and supported by evidence: Yarn/Bun workspaces, Turborepo, Nx, Lage, API Extractor, tsup, Rollup, unbuild, Vitest, Playwright, Changesets, semantic-release, Registry-based installation, and static documentation tools. Do not pick every tool in this list. They are candidates to assess, not mandatory dependencies.

### Research rules

- Primary docs/release notes beat blogs and examples.
- Community posts may reveal usability problems, but label them as anecdotal.
- Verify the current generation of `shadcn` registry format/schema and whether the feature is appropriate for this repo’s intended consumers.
- Do not assume the registry is identical to publishing a conventional npm package. Compare source-owned/installable code against runtime dependency packages as distinct distribution models.
- Do not choose Node or npm versions by trend. Derive supported ranges from the current repo and the needs of consumers, then document evidence and migration risk.
- Do not claim trademark clearance, npm scope availability, or legal safety. These require separate verification.
- Record research sources in `docs/research/package-architecture-dx-research-log.md` or a suitable existing canonical file; do not duplicate research notes across many docs.

