## 10. Phase 9 — Monorepo, build graph, and dependency management

Only recommend a monorepo when it creates measurable value.

Research and compare appropriate options based on the actual repository: npm workspaces, pnpm workspaces, Yarn, Bun, or no workspace. Evaluate Turbo/Nx/task runners only if task dependency/caching complexity warrants them.

Specify:

- workspace naming and folder conventions;
- package dependency graph and forbidden cycles;
- single source of truth for versions/configs;
- package scripts (build, typecheck, lint, test, validate, pack, docs, changeset/release);
- development order and watch mode;
- generated code/token build dependencies;
- incremental versus full CI;
- task caching and reproducibility where relevant;
- local/CI Node and package-manager version pinning;
- lockfile policy and dependency update policy;
- dependency graph visualization/auditing;
- how examples consume workspace packages without masking publication defects.

Test planning must include a clean consumer installation from the packed tarball, not only workspace aliases. Workspace symlinks can hide missing files and wrong export maps.

