## 11. Phase 10 — Versioning, releases, and supply-chain safety

Research current official guidance for npm Trusted Publishing/OIDC, provenance attestations, GitHub Actions permissions, release tags, Changesets or alternatives, and dependency security.

Specify:

- package versioning model (single version or independent versions), with evidence;
- conventional version/semver rules for components, tokens, theme contract schema, registry items and docs examples;
- changeset/release note workflow;
- changelog format and migration guide policy;
- release candidate and smoke-test stages;
- publish permissions and protected branch/tag policy;
- trusted publishing vs long-lived npm tokens, current requirements and caveats;
- provenance/SBOM/attestation requirements where justified;
- lockfile integrity and dependency review;
- actions pinning/permissions/secrets minimization;
- package tarball inspection and `npm pack --dry-run`/equivalent validation;
- npm package metadata correctness;
- rollback, deprecation and incident response;
- prerelease tags (`alpha`, `beta`, `rc`) and promotion rules;
- how docs match the published package version;
- whether package publication is v1 scope or later.

Do not configure npm publishing, create secrets, run a release, or publish any package. This phase is only the policy and workflow specification. Do not claim provenance is available for a proposed package before the eligible publishing/repository configuration is verified.

