## 14. Scope boundaries with adjacent Moonframe Bibles

This work must integrate with—rather than duplicate—the following areas:

- **Design System Bible:** product mission, principles, scope and 15-skin catalog.
- **Token Architecture & Theme Engine Bible:** token semantics, source of truth, Light/Dark resolver, runtime theme behavior.
- **Component API & Behavior Bible:** component props, interaction semantics, keyboard/ARIA contracts and state matrix.
- **Premium Blocks & Template Product Bible:** catalog and requirements of blocks/templates.
- **Advanced Data Workspace Bible:** detailed table/data workspace semantics and adapter contracts.
- **Auth & Security UI Integration Bible:** auth UI flows/provider boundaries.
- **Original Asset & Brand Bible:** asset taxonomy, originality, license and provenance.
- **Motion, Interaction & SFX Bible:** motion recipe and audio-event semantics.
- **Accessibility & Visual QA Bible:** accessibility and visual-regression gates.

Do not copy their full catalog/details into this document. Package Architecture & DX should define **how those systems are packaged, imported, installed, documented, tested, versioned, and released**. Link to canonical docs and capture only package-level dependencies/requirements.

Where adjacent Bibles do not exist or are incomplete, record a dependency/gap rather than creating a duplicate competing source of truth. Add an index or master map only if absent.

